<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="WFInfo.Linux.Views.WelcomeDialogue"
        Title="Welcome to WFInfo"
        Width="390" Height="330"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        Background="#FF1B1B1B"
        CanResize="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="Manual">
    <Grid PointerPressed="Grid_PointerPressed">
        <Border BorderBrush="#FF707070" BorderThickness="1">
            <StackPanel>
                <!-- Title bar -->
                <Grid Height="26" Background="#FF0F0F0F">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="4,0,0,0">
                        <Image Source="avares://WFInfo.Linux/Resources/WFLogo.png" Height="20" Width="20" Margin="0,0,4,0"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="WFInfo" FontSize="14" FontWeight="Bold" FontFamily="{StaticResource RobotoBlack}" Foreground="#FFB1D0D9" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                    <Button Content="x" Click="Exit_Click"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                            Background="Transparent" Foreground="#FFB1D0D9"
                            Width="29" Height="26" FontSize="14"
                            HorizontalContentAlignment="Center" VerticalContentAlignment="Center"/>
                </Grid>

                <!-- Welcome text -->
                <TextBlock Text="Welcome to WFInfo!" FontSize="18"
                           Foreground="#FFB1D0D9" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                           Margin="0,8,0,0"/>

                <!-- Guide text -->
                <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Foreground="#FFB1D0D9" FontSize="13"
                           Margin="20,10,20,0" LineHeight="18">
Here's a quick guide on how to get started

First go into Settings and verify the following:
  • Overlay will overlay the results on top of Warframe
  • Window will make it display elsewhere, like a 2nd monitor
  • Light will make a sound and copy to clipboard
  • Activation Key is the key that will trigger the display

Linux-specific notes:
  • Run with --setup-input for reliable global hotkeys
  • Warframe runs via Steam Proton (borderless window)
  • Log out and back in after setup for input group changes

After these have been checked, you should be good!

To use Snap-it, press Ctrl + activation key, then
drag a rectangle over the items you want to scan.

If you need help, we're active in Discord!
                </TextBlock>
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>
    </Grid>
</Window>